+{"connection_id":"BC-b73eb2c58254308a311a","ref":"WLC:1Kgs.19.18","status":"accepted","reason":"God leaves seven thousand who have not bowed to Baal, a morally defined surviving group.","paragraphs":[62],"evidence":["WLC:Zeph.3.12","WLC:Zeph.3.13","WLC:1Kgs.19.18","WLC:Amos.5.15"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b860e30a6ee1428ae32d","ref":"WLC:1Kgs.19.18","status":"accepted","reason":"The remnant is specified by not worshiping Baal, as the annotation explains.","paragraphs":[62],"evidence":["WLC:Zeph.3.12","WLC:Zeph.3.13","WLC:1Kgs.19.18","WLC:Amos.5.15"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-22d6421f8f0daf5e2586","ref":"WLC:1Kgs.3.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Solomon requests discernment rather than riches or long life, but this wisdom-for-judgment choice lacks the afterlife and refuse contrast.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:1Kgs.3.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-96c7bf8c1787ddc16c2e","ref":"WLC:1Sam.16.7","status":"rejected","reason":"God's seeing the heart rather than appearance is true, but the verse concerns selection of a king, not lowly people or enduring goods.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:1Sam.16.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-9b6dffb84a1e0e8b713a","ref":"WLC:Amos.5.15","status":"accepted","reason":"Amos couples love of good and public justice with hope for grace toward Joseph's remnant.","paragraphs":[62],"evidence":["WLC:Zeph.3.12","WLC:Zeph.3.13","WLC:1Kgs.19.18","WLC:Amos.5.15"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fe8dc7524107474b086c","ref":"WLC:Dan.12.2","status":"accepted","reason":"Some awake to everlasting life and some to everlasting contempt, showing permanence on both sides.","paragraphs":[64],"evidence":["WLC:Dan.12.2","WLC:Eccl.3.21","WLC:Eccl.9.5"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-008"]}
